WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
<b>Drawing Fun!</b>

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:01.860
Drawing!

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.050
F - U - N !

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.540
Big sister, big sister!

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.540
Oh! This big sister is different from usual!

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:08.950
Nice to meet you.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.590
Oh, no! Did it already start?

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.590
GA's already started.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.750
I'm sorry, I got here late.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.090
Kisaragi, I can't see!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.480
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.820
Kisaragi, watch out! 
That's gonna fall!

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.470
Hold on.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.980
I'll clean it up, so can you get
 something to wipe this up with?

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.860
Ah-ha! It's you again, Yamaguchi-san.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:00.850
This makes how many times?

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.790
I-I think it might be the third time...

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.600
You've aleady broken that many?

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.110
Oh crap! Professor Sotoma is here!

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:10.360
Something to wipe this up with!

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.000
Another cup! Another cup!

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.440
You guys!

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.870
Why are you making

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.810
little urine-sample cups on my desk?

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.460
<b>Life Art</b>

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.190
 Staff Room

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.190
Sorry!

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.340
Actually, Professor, 
don't you think your desk

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.000
is a little too cluttered?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.030
You always leave your coffee here, too!

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:33.800
That's right!

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.400
There's nowhere to put our assignments.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.230
Yes, yes.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.970
Your professor isn't angry,
 so show me your assignments.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.970
Today's Assignment

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.090
This might be a little harsh, but it's plain.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.460
To be honest, when I think of a vacuum cleaner

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.380
that's all that comes into my head.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.780
Namiko-san, you're too rigid!

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.770
You're still young, so you gotta
 give your mind some freedom!

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.920
Freedom, huh?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.750
Speaking of which, Tomokane, 
what is this supposed to be?

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.390
I said it had to be an everyday tool.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:58.160
Huh?

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.740
That's a vacuum cleaner, too.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.660
You're giving yourself too much freedom!

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.450
What was the assignment?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.460
To design an everyday tool.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:07.800
What about you, Yamaguchi?

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.470
Y- Yes... um...

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.400
<b>Flip  Flip</b>

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.640
Kisaragi, Kisaragi.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.240
You're the same as Nozaki.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.340
This is a design, so try to have a little more fun.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.180
For example, take this cell phone.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.910
If you combined this with something you liked,

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.140
how would you design it?

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:33.740
 Phone, phone...

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:34.840
Poink

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:41.950
Ooh, she's blossoming.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.980
All right, then you two try a little harder on this, too.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.120
You can come up with something better, right?

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.300
Hold on a minute!

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.330
I didn't hear anything about a redo!

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.410
Stingy! That's stingy!

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.310
Sotoma's class sure is energetic.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.310
Stingy stingy stingy stingy stingy!

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.240
Professor Sotoma.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.090
This is a staff room, so please,

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.500
could you keep your voices down?

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.090
Oh, yes. Excuse us.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.590
Remember this, Professor.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.590
You'll regrate setting 
fire to my artistic soul!

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.590
You'll regrate setting 
fire to my artistic soul!

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:08.000
It's "regret".

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.590
It's "regret".

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.360
Excuse me.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.730
Oh, Oomichi, you already turned yours in, right?

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.630
I brought someone.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.810
Professor, I brought it.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.740
Noda, you haven't turned yours in yet?

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.480
How unusual. 
This is your specialty, right?

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.280
I'm a little sleepy today.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.570
But don't worry.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.930
The god of design descended on me just now.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:35.490
Oomichi, throw some water on 
her face and bring her back.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.870
Excuse me.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:38.920
Yamaguchi?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.980
I'm here to resubmit my design.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:43.360
Excuse me!

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.760
Tomokane, I really am going to excuse you.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.130
Professor! Professor!

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.670
I feel really good about this one.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:51.170
It might even succeed as a real product!

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.540
Really? Show me.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.860
It's called the "Make-even-a-cluttered-desk-look-clean cover"!

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.280
Yamaguchi, show me yours.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.310
Oh, here.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.540
This is definitely your characteristic style.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.980
But for a design, it's a little childish.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.660
Looks like a grade schooler's product.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:12.830
If you give it a few more 
tries, it might get better.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.060
Also, this is number four.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:16.960
Ahh!

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.610
I'm going to get some coffee... 
in a borrowed mug.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.740
Maybe you should take a break
 in the lounge for a moment.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:25.650
Excuse me!

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.650
Take a look at this, Chief!

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.840
Who is this "Chief"?

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.820
This time I've done it for sure, Chief!

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.610
A presentation?

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.470
I heard that this idea was a big hit.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:39.750
<b> Would you be interested in...</b>

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:39.750
 Flipable
 Desk

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:39.750
Instant 
Storage!!

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:36.980
If you're applying for a patent,

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.650
go to the licensing department, 
not the staff room.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:40.220
<b> Ta-da!</b>

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.380
And, if you order today,

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.480
you'll get this Desk Cover absolutely free!

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.070
What a bargain!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.260
Aren't we getting a little off topic here?

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.620
Professor! Professor! 
Then what about this one?!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.170
I've got a lot of confidence in this one!

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.260
Fine, fine. Let's see it. 
Just do as you please.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.770
 Future Desk

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:00.470
Professor, this time I'm completely awake.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.460
You again?

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:01.770
 Super Future Desk

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.970
All of you, go back and redo it!

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.940
Professor Sotoma! I told you already!

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.780
Ahh! All right! I'm sorry!

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.280
Man, they really wear me out.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.130
What's this?

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.420
Oh, Yamaguchi-san was just here.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.060
I told her that you were 
going to be right back.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.840
But she just left like she was
 running away from something.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.560
Do they hate me now?

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.070
Since you were gone,
 I had her show it to me.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:33.670
A soft mug?

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.920
This design is really interesting;

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.940
do you think it would
 be a better insulator?

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.450
Oh, no.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.200
Actually, I thought of it

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.740
while I was watching 
Professor Sotoma drink coffee.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.300
Um, it might just be me,

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.930
but I find that soft things 
really help me to relax, so...

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.440
This is exactly the kind of design
 I'd expect from you, Yamaguchi-san.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:54.710
Personally,

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.180
I thought it would be nice

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.510
if there was a cup that 
didn't break when dropped.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.870
A very Yamaguchi-san way of thinking.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.820
I think Professor Sotoma would
 be very happy to hear that.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.240
Oh, no! It's okay.
 Please don't tell him!

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.810
I ended up telling you anyway!

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.730
They may be a handful,

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:16.230
but I think that your students respect you a lot.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.320
It would be nice if it was true.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.220
I hope I become someone
 people can depend on soon.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.190
Chief!

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:24.930
You guys!

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.620
Sotoma!

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.950
I'm returning last week's assignments.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:33.610
<i>To learn art and design is to draw</i>

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.810
Someone looks happy.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.950
<i>upon the character that is in each and every one of us.</i>

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.270
Professor Sotoma, question!

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.800
<i>That's why it's difficult to learn...</i>

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.770
What is it?

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.860
What did I design, exactly?

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.160
Remember yourself.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.670
If you can't remember, I'm reducing your grade by half.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.410
<i>...and also maybe why it's difficult to teach.</i>

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.940
What is this?

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:49.910
Remember!

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:54.920
<b>The Coffee Cup History of Professor Sotoma.</b>

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:50.880
<b>1st Generation</b>

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:51.930
<b>2nd Generation</b>

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:52.930
<b>3rd Generation</b>

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:53.770
<b>4th Generation</b>

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:54.200
<b>Unusable</b>

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:54.920
<b>5th Generation (Temporary), School Soup Bowl</b>

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:58.870
Here she comes!

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.620
She's here?

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.610
Namiko-san!

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.890
Here! Congratulations!

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:08.210
I'm surprised you knew, Kisaragi!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.240
What, what? What is that for?

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:15.710
She's the 5 millionth person to enter this room!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.160
<b> Winner!</b>

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:16.520
So lucky...

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.620
That's ridiculous!

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.340
Oh, so today's your birthday!

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.780
You should have told me yesterday!

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.590
Don't worry about it.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.130
I don't really celebrate 
other people's birthdays either.

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.710
Namiko-san! Namiko-san, here!

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.250
I just made this for you!

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.260
<b> "Good for anything" Coupon.
 Usable today only.</b>

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.030
It's perishable, so please 
use it as soon as possible.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:38.900
Perishable?

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.400
<b><i>Today's Perishable Food</i></b>

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.080
It's only good today!

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:43.710
Kyouju and I just talked about it

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:44.770
and we decided

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.670
that we should do something for your birthday.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.430
So, after school today,

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.730
we'll buy some sweets and some drinks

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.180
and have a small party!

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.180
Here?

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:58.970
So just what we normally do,
 but under a different name.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.540
Actually, Noda-dono originally wanted

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.530
to hop between restaurants
that offer freebies on birthdays endlessly

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.250
to another restaurant endlessly...

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.630
And just eat free desserts and take photos all day!

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:12.960
Oh, I spoke too soon. 
The school is just fine.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.400
You two, this way!

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.310
 Art Room

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.310
Oh! Are we having it in the art room?

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.820
Since we're having a birthday party,

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.310
I thought we'd do something different.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.330
I invited all the ladies and gentlemen.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:34.080
Hey Brutus, why are you facing that way?

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.840
Isn't it obvious?

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.040
Namiko-dono's smile is far too brilliant, Apollo-dono.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.590
You guys! Even role-playing has limits!

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.530
In celebration of Namiko-san's birthday...

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.030
Cheers!

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.100
You're already turning sixteen before any of us.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:51.680
Any plans for a boyfriend?

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:53.370
Are you trying to start a fight?

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:56.940
I feel like you or Masa will 
probably get one first anyway.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.240
Kyouju-san, apparently you're quite popular

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.070
with the other classes, right?

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.710
I don't have a boyfriend,

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.550
but it seems my parents have chosen a fiancé for me.

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:07.020
Oh, is that so?!

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.790
Did we just hear something amazing?!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.860
Hey, is it just me or does anyone else wonder:

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.860
And? What kind of person is he?

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:17.360
(ale = eeru = cheer)

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:17.360
Who is ginger ale cheering for?

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:18.810
Not really.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:19.610
Is that so...

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:20.640
Thank you.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.570
Ever thought about who fruit punch is punching?

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:25.870
Don't think so.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.370
<b> Sour Redbean Soup</b>

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.880
Kyouju-san, don't you dislike that drink?

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.900
Oh, then we must've 
bought it without thinking.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:34.880
Sorry about that.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:38.220
So, can one of you go get us a new one?

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.520
Huh? It's so far.

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:43.060
Hey Namiko-san, don't you think 
we should decide with rock-paper--

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:48.730
Damn it! I should've given her massage coupons!

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:52.530
I bought them.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:54.370
About time.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.060
Which one is Oolong tea?

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:57.880
This one.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.750
So tired...

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.990
Since when did this 
become so chemically unnatural?

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.620
Turn around, the dark alchemist is leering at you.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.420
Sorry, Kisaragi.
 You're dripping wet.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:15.520
No, it's not your fault, Tomokane-san.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.570
You can change over there.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.820
We'll all face the other way.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:20.790
Sorry for the trouble.

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:23.010
Do we have anything to wipe this up with?

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.800
Noda, you better feel bad about this.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.300
Twitch  Twitch

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.330
Whoever loses at Rock-Paper-Scissors
 has to carry the bag, okay?

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.660
So I'm already sixteen?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:36.640
Are you worried?

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:38.760
It's just that hanging out with them

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.280
makes me feel really old.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.820
Heavy! You're heavy!

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.000
Excuse me.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.660
Oh yeah, I haven't opened 
Kisaragi's present yet.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:55.660
From the size of it, it looks like it
 could be a book or a sketchbook.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:02.030
 Dear Namiko-san,
You're always working so hard.
Take a break sometime 
and read this book.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:02.030
The White Piggie's Pancakes

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.320
I see.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.640
It's not that I'm an adult.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.520
It's just that they're exceedingly childish.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:09.320
Chief!

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:13.040
<b> Dean of Students</b>

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:13.040
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.000
You guys!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Sotoma!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:18.050
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:18.050
Bunny Cell Phone

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:18.050
 Bzz bzz bzzz

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:16.670
Phonecall! Phonecall! Charging...

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.050
Ooh, she's blossoming!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:21.750
Is Aa-san not here?

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.520
Hey, you're being called.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.690
 President's Cottage

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.160
President's Cottage?

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:31.860
I didn't know we had one.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.010
It's great, right?

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.500
Tono made it for me and
 it comes with a blanket!

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.520
Oh yeah, by the way, 
are you still president?

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.760
Since we merged with
 the School Lifestyle Club,

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.970
Mizubuchi's also a president.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.400
I don't mind.
 Aa-san can be president.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.660
I had no club members,

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.050
so I was only ever a president in name.

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.210
Buchi-san!

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.230
However, I am disposing of this cottage.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.560
I see.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.560
She's in a position of greater
 authority than the president.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:02.830
Now's a good time.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.340
Let's clean up the club room.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:06.630
Right now?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:10.240
But Buchi-san, Professor Tono still isn't here.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.400
Oh, Tono. Speak of the devil.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.020
She was planning

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.620
on secretly smoking in
 here again, wasn't she?

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.660
It must be two hours since her last smoke.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:23.850
From the way she looked,
 she won't be back for some time.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.750
So, let's get started.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.220
What a drag.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.120
You're the president, so act like one.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.100
Okay, okay.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.260
So we'll leave the brooms and mops to the boys and...

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.800
That won't do, they'll just mess around.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.350
So instead of brooms, if we give them rags...

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:42.480
That won't work either...

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.940
The only thing I can give them...

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.280
Here! Sweep the floor with this.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.410
That's tiny!

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.770
You want us to sweep with a brush.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.960
Let's see, this one is still good.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:57.300
This acrylic is dry so we can't use it.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.280
Can't use this one either.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.890
Is this all the usable paint we have?

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:04.600
I thought we had a lot more,

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.950
like ones that the graduated students left behind.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.360
We might have to talk about buying more supplies...

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:12.120
But do we have enough club funds?

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.470
There's no need for that.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:17.990
There were plenty of usable paints in the president's cottage.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.390
Mostly unused ones.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.120
Well, well.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:23.070
Good thing we decided to clean.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.210
Who knows what else might turn up.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:27.120
Whose textbook is this?

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.720
Uozumi, have you been studying in here again?

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:35.290
 Mathematics III

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.520
This textbook is really different from mine,

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:34.400
even though we're in the same year.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:35.290
Is that so?

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:37.970
Whaa... even the text inside is really small

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.290
and hard to read.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:44.060
Why are there two math textbooks... 3 and C?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.240
Whose textbook is this?

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.430
Oh, that's mine.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.070
Why did you leave it in the club room?

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.360
They're all specialty subjects.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.350
Design, Architecture...

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:55.910
I have normal textbooks as well.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.110
Ahh, this is for English.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.410
Wait, are you a third year middle schooler?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.130
Wrong. Why are you adjusting your glasses?

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.200
How rude.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.580
I'm going to clean up over there.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:10.390
It was over here!

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:12.990
The Honda Mai art book that I thought I lost!

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.050
Hurray for club room clean up!

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.160
Honda Mai?

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.760
Aa-san's favorite modern artist.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:23.400
After I graduate, going to an art college,

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.270
gaining experience, and becoming an apprentice

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.830
to this person is my dream!

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.620
Apprentice?

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.580
What does an artist's apprentice do?

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.580
Get a name like Honda Teichikahei or something.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.540
Not that kind of apprentice!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:36.070
What's this?

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:38.980
A juice can in a place like this?

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:41.580
Hey, can I drink this?

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.490
Oh, that?

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.390
If you wanna drink it, 
then go right ahead!

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:47.910
Aa-san! Be a little responsible!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:49.890
Homura-kun! Don't drink that!

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.080
That's used as a sketch model

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.360
so it's at least ten years past its best by date!

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:56.920
Now that you mention it,

00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:00.340
I haven't seen a pull-tab 
canned juice since I was a kid.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.740
I'm nearly spent from all this tiring cleaning up!

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.740
(Erai = Tiring)

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:05.790
You're right.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.330
Aa-san, for a sloth, you sure are working hard.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.190
Admirable!

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.190
(Erai = Admirable)

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.400
(Erai = Tiring)

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.400
Aren't you all tired, too?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.380
We're working really hard after school.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.230
Well, if you go by position,

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:15.760
I say the president is most admirable.

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:15.760
(Erai = Admirable)

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.900
"Erai"... I guess so...

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:20.580
Stop complaining about how tired you are

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.810
and finish cleaning up!

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:27.880
Let me drink some.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:28.840
You can have it all.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.680
I don't want all of it.

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:32.620
Is Professor Sasamoto out?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.400
Professor Same-chan!

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.490
She's probably in the teachers' lounge.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.070
I see.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.570
Wahh who?! Who is that?!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.140
 Who?

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:41.710
Professor Same-chan. She teaches painting.

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:42.680
Same?

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.250
2 Years Ago

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.180
 Usami

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.190
I-I'm pleased to meet everyone!

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:54.460
<b> Clack  Clack</b>

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.480
GA students, s-starting this s-semester

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:54.460
I'll be t-teaching painting.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.590
I'm U-Usame Mayumi!

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.890
U..same?

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.890
Damn it!

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.210
Can't you guys share some of those teachers

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:04.720
with the automobile maintenance courses?

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.560
I'm starting to really look forward

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.180
to coming to this building!

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.480
It must be nice to be simple.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.680
This time it's Professor Sotoma!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.420
I need some sample presentation materials.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:20.480
Could you open up the back room for me?

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:23.540
The back room!

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.090
N-No one but Tono can survive back there!

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.690
Well, please do something about it, and quickly.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:30.960
What's going on?

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.830
Buchi-san, if I don't return,

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:35.560
I'd like a small grave

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:37.340
under the zelkova tree in the inner courtyard,

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:39.380
and don't forget the flower...

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:40.570
Where is the back room?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.220
Hey, there was a door back there?

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:47.660
Normally, we don't go in it, so...

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.490
I'll be going now...

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:51.410
Why are you crying?

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:58.590
<b>NO ENTRY</b>

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.590
<b> Bam!</b>

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.090
<b> Crash!</b>

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.090
<b> Thunk!</b>

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.590
<b> Gaaah!</b>

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:06.350
We got it.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.230
Where does that door lead?

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.640
It's connected to another art room,

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:15.780
but it hasn't been used for a long time.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.410
Now it's a storage space,

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:18.660
or rather, a chaotic space

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.640
filled with old pieces of 
work and teaching materials.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:22.520
In the past, every fine arts club member

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.050
had to endure the gauntlet of that room.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:27.920
Maybe that's why there aren't
 many club members anymore.

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:31.560
A few years ago, a strange thing happened.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:35.000
One club member entered that room alone,

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.700
in search of some reference materials.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:39.250
But when he opened the door and walked out,

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.430
the form of a girl was clinging to his back!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:46.090
Since then, that girl has become a sketch model here.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:47.600
So it was Sanae-chan!

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:51.210
 Redbean Soup Drink

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:51.210
Officially, it's Professor Tono's responsibility,

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:54.150
but she isn't the type to do anything about it.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.660
The other teachers are too scared to go in.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.900
I feel like I understand why

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.220
you were given this room as your club room.

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:05.660
Apparently, it was originally a GC classroom.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.710
Since Sanae-chan was in there,

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:09.370
maybe it was a fashion design class.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:10.460
GC?

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.430
Then there used to be three Geijutsu classes?

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.080
Even after being here for three years,

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.070
there are still rooms that I don't know about.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:18.170
I am so surprised!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:21.590
I'm not the president here for nothing.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:25.210
The supply room has always been my responsibility.

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:29.750
Oh!

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:32.330
Looks prettier somehow.

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.780
You're finally back.

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:38.090
Wasn't there something there before?

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:39.590
The President's cottage.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.230
Did you really make that for her?

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:44.080
Well... yeah.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:49.180
Back then she was always alone.

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:51.740
It was before Homura came

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:54.290
and after all the other upperclassmen left.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:57.320
Uozumi stopped coming, too.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:58.920
But, she was always ready

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.440
in case someone decided to come to the club,

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.280
ready to start the club at anytime.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.170
Every week, every time, she'd be here.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.130
Get inside here.

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:09.060
She was annoying so I quarantined her.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.960
So, basically, that cottage was just for your convenience!

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:15.860
Well, I did use it a lot.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.660
When I was alone, there was too much room

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:19.150
and it felt so uncomfortable.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.380
Even though the room was filled with all kinds of junk.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:27.840
So, that's why throwing it away seems a little wasteful.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.180
There, there. No use thinking about it.

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:32.810
You don't need it anymore, right?

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:35.050
You have a club full of people

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.530
who look after their president now.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:41.250
Buchi-san, you really are admirable, huh?

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:43.870
You're right,

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:45.090
it sure is tiring having a friend

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.530
who needs you by her side all the time!

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:50.820
I didn't mean it that way, this time!

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:55.530
Oh, is Aa-san out again?

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:58.300
Awara? She's been over there the whole time.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:05.210
Sleeping Sweetly

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:05.210
She sure does look comfortable under there.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:09.380
It is said that, on that day, 
a new Presidential Box was created.

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:15.090
It's turned into a real downpour!

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.560
Shoot! I forgot my umbrella!

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:18.220
How about you guys?

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:19.490
I brought mine.

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:20.520
I'm not in the habit of using one.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:22.010
I'm in the habit of sharing someone else's!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.950
Don't be proud of that!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:25.500
Oh, don't worry.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.230
I have one that I bought just yesterday.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.150
It should fit two or three-

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:35.530
Kisaragi-chan is putting away her umbrella

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:36.610
like it never even happened!

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:37.440
You brat!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.180
Grab her arms and steal that umbrella!

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:40.360
Well then, I'll be going.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.010
You're leaving?

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:42.790
Kisaragi-chan's moving quickly!

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:44.540
You won't escape!

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:46.420
It's raining pretty hard...

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:47.940
Let's go as well.

00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:49.500
If we stay under the trees

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.550
until we get to the bus stop,
 we should be fine.

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:55.030
It'll work out, I guess.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:28.240
Eek! I just heard a really high pitched scream!

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.180
Professor Usami appears to have been very surprised.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:31.250
But what surprised her?

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:33.360
Art Room 2 is in trouble!

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:34.990
How much? How much for one?

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:36.060
Where should I put the money?

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:39.390
The only opponent I can't lay my hands on...

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:40.060
The Haunted Art Room
